-- title:
--   Lifting finite places to Q​; pointwise constant reductions
-- statement:
--   For an intermediate field $L$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ that is a number field and a finite place $\nu$ of $L$, [`ModularCurve.nuBall`](../def/ModularCurve_FinitePlaceLift.html#L18) is the valuation subring $\{a \in L : \nu(a) \le 1\}$ of $L$; its units are exactly the $a$ with $\nu(a)=1$ and its maximal ideal is $\{\nu(a)<1\}$ (`nuBallOpen` is that ideal, viewed inside `nuBall`). The structure [`ModularCurve.FinitePlaceLift L ν`](../def/ModularCurve_FinitePlaceLift.html#L78) packages a lift of $\nu$ to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose field `mem_iff` asserts that for all $a \in L$ one has $a \in A$ iff $\nu(a) \le 1$, together with a natural number $p$, a proof that $p$ is prime, and a proof of `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p \in A^{\mathrm{nonunits}}$. The accompanying lemmas identify, for $a \in L$ lying in $A$, invertibility in $A$ with $\nu(a)=1$ and membership in $\mathfrak m_A$ with $\nu(a)<1$; they give $\operatorname{char} \kappa(A) = p$ and $\nu(p)<1$, and produce the ring homomorphism `traceHom` from `nuBall` to $A$ (inclusion on elements) together with the induced map `residueFieldEmb` of residue fields. Existence of a lift (`exists_finitePlaceLift`, `nonempty_finitePlaceLift`) comes from exhibiting a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose trace on $L$ is the $\nu$-unit ball, obtained by dominating the image of `nuBallOpen` under the inclusion $L \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and from a rational prime $q$ with $\nu(q)<1$.
--
--   The second part adds two predicates on a `ConstantReduction R` of $F/K$ along a valuation subring $A$ of $K$. `IsPointwise` says: for every place $P$ of $F/K$ whose residue field is generated by $K$ (`IsRational`) and every $f$ in $R$'s ring of integers which lies in the valuation subring of every place $w$ with $R.\mathrm{placeMap}(w)=R.\mathrm{placeMap}(P)$, the reduction $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation subring of $R.\mathrm{placeMap}(P)$, the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$, and the image of its residue under $\kappa(A) \to \kappa(R.\mathrm{placeMap}(P))$ is the residue of $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$. `IsDiscParam R P T` says $T$ lies in the integers, its reduction is nonzero and has order exactly $1$ at $R.\mathrm{placeMap}(P)$, $P.\mathrm{ord}(T) > 0$, and $Q.\mathrm{ord}(T) \ge 0$ for every $Q$ in the fibre of $P$ under $R.\mathrm{placeMap}$. Both hold for the degenerate reduction `ofTop`, built from $A = \top$: there the residue field of $\top$ is identified with $L$ by `residueTopEquiv`, $F$ carries the induced algebra structure, the integers are all of $F$, the residue map is the identity inclusion, and `placeMap` is the resulting bijection between places (`placeMapOfTop`, shown injective and surjective, order-preserving on `ord`). In addition `Place L L` is empty, so `ofTop L L` is pointwise for that reason as well, and irreducible elements of a place's valuation ring give disc parameters for `ofTop`.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib supplies `ValuationSubring`, `NumberField.FinitePlace` and the residue-field machinery; `nuBall` assembles the $\nu$-unit ball as a valuation subring of $L$. The structure `FinitePlaceLift`, the predicate `LiesOverPrime`, and the reduction notions `ConstantReduction`, `IsPointwise` and `IsDiscParam` are the project's own; Mathlib has no notion of constant reduction of function fields.
--
--   **Where it is used.** The lifting of a finite place of a number field to a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with prescribed residue characteristic is the vocabulary in which reduction of curves over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and inertia at a finite place are stated in the later modules; the constant-reduction predicates fix the language used for pointwise reduction of functions on modular curves.
-- source:
